spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:96:| FR-004 | Cross-tab ordering and ownership: the outbox order 
is shared by all tabs; per conversation, only the oldest unresolved item is eligible, and at most one tab holds the 
conversation's drain claim at a time (atomic claim). A claim is a lease: it ends when its tab closes or crashes, or 
when its holder exceeds the attempt deadline (request timeout 30 s; lease 45 s), and another tab then resumes after 
fencing (FR-006). When connectivity returns, an attempt that started before or during the outage is superseded 
immediately (fenced and redispatched under a new generation by whichever tab drains), so a hung holder never delays 
the D1 deadline. Across all tabs, no two create requests of the same conversation's outbox are in progress at once. | 
Must | AC-005, AC-041 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:111:| FR-019 | Typing signals travel only on a private Realtime 
topic whose join and send are authorized for current conversation members; anon clients, authenticated non-members, 
and public-topic attempts never receive them; the app detects the user's own removal from a conversation through a 
signal that does not depend on still having access to that conversation and leaves the topic within 5 s. Payload: user 
identity and typing flag only. Residual risk accepted (D3, D6): a tampered client of a removed member may receive and 
send typing signals until its access token expires. | Must | AC-019 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:117:| FR-025 | With the Phase 4 desktop-notification toggle on and 
permission granted, a mentioned user receives one desktop notification for a message that mentions them (direct, 
group, room, thread reply), titled "<Autor> mencionou você em <conversa>" with the full text; clicking opens the 
conversation. Before emitting, the app confirms with authoritative data, under the current identity, that the user is 
still a member and (for rooms) mentioned; then, with no further awaits before display, it re-checks that the same user 
is still signed in and that no removal signal for that conversation has arrived; otherwise the pending notification is 
discarded, as it is on any account switch or sign-out. Residual race accepted (D6): a removal that the app has not yet 
received when the final check runs may let that one notification show. Suppression is browser-wide: no tab notifies if 
any of the user's tabs in that browser is visible and viewing that conversation, regardless of which tab receives the 
event first. | Must | AC-025, AC-026, AC-049 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:140:| BR-009 | Typing: only current conversation members join and 
send on a conversation's typing topic; a user's own typing (any session) is never shown to them; an indicator expires 
≤ 5 s after the last signal; the app leaves a conversation's topic within 5 s of the user's removal; residual exposure 
(receive and send) of a tampered removed-member client is bounded by access-token lifetime (D3, D6). | R1-q8 A, D, E; 
R1-q16 E; D3; D6 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:142:| BR-011 | Desktop-notification eligibility (extends Phase 4): 
toggle on and permission granted; never for the user's own message; the same user must still be signed in and a member 
at emission time (final check without intervening awaits; residual race accepted, D6); never while any tab of the user 
in that browser is visible and viewing that conversation; DM/group: every new message; room: only messages that 
mention the user; at most one notification per message per browser. | R1-q10 B, R1-q16 C/F, R2-q8 A, R2-q9 A–C; 
reviews r2 #9, r3 #3 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:192:| Hung holder when connectivity returns | Its attempt is 
superseded at once; D1 deadline holds (AC-041). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:194:| Owning tab closes or hangs mid-request | Closed or lease 
expired: another tab fences and finishes once; while the lease is live no other tab dispatches (AC-041). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:216:| Recipient removed or account switched after commit but 
before the notification is shown | No notification once the app has the removal/switch signal; a removal not yet 
received at the final check is the accepted D6 race (AC-049). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:219:| Hidden tab receives a mention event first while another tab 
views that conversation | No notification (AC-026). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:227:- Typing topics are private and members-only for join and send 
