401-- Enqueue: refuse non-UUID or known cross-conversation reply target before any write → commit → publish the 
committed item into the pending query (re-read best effort) → composer clears. D5: indexedDB missing / open fails / 
write aborts → nothing dispatched, text + reply kept, alert "Este navegador não permite guardar mensagens; libere o 
armazenamento do site".
402-- Drain: triggers load, enqueue, `online` (resets backoff), backoff 1→15 s; per conversation one loop per tab + 
Web Lock `vo-messaging-outbox:<users.id>:<conversationId>` (ifAvailable); claim oldest atomically (generation+1); 
nothing claimed while offline; failed/expired oldest blocks the conversation (BR-003). Dispatch carries 
clientMessageId, attemptGeneration, expectedSenderId (users.id), mentionIds only when non-empty. Outcomes: 200/201 
confirm only when `parseStoredMessage` (outbox-ack.ts) validates correlation (UUID id, senderId, conversationId, key) 
and every rendered field (content string, replyToId null/UUID, timestamp, type, status, isEdited, reactions, 
mentionedUserIds, readCount; attachments empty) and builds the Message from validated fields only — stored 
content/replyToId may legitimately differ from the item; 410 MESSAGE_DELETED → delivered; 429/401 → waiting; 
network/5xx/any non-confirming 2xx → unknown; 409 ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED → unknown if still this tab's claim; other 4xx → 
failed. Unknown and orphaned claimed items redispatch at generation+1 without a fence (exactly-once by T2 server 
fence-on-create + key uniqueness; review r1 confirmed). Labels: pendente / enviando / não enviada / expirada.
